The key points to consider for writing the clinical case about 'Lymphadenectomy after a breast-conserving approach in early-stage unilateral breast carcinoma with lymph node involvement' are as follows:
Patient Information: Name: DELANNOY Paulette; Date of birth: 09/11/1953; Age: 66 years old.
Diagnostic Findings: Pathologic T stage: T1; Pathologic N stage: N1; Overall pathologic stage: IIA; Histological grade: SBR II; Tumor size: 15 mm; Estrogen receptors status: Positive; Progesterone receptors status: Positive; Number of axillary nodes examined: 2; Number of positive axillary nodes: 1.
Therapeutic Context: Surgical treatment according to T1N1M0 classification; Administration of adjuvant therapies based on ER and PR status; Decision made at multidisciplinary meeting.
Treatment Planning: Dosimetric computed tomography (CTDI); Planned delivered dose (PDL); Dosimetry techniques;
Radiotherapy Characteristics: Start and end dates; Fractionation scheme; Accelerator characteristics (energy, type); Target volumes; Total and fractional prescribed doses; Average and maximum doses; Contraintes on organs at risk (OAR) with tolerance levels indicated within parentheses (e.g., lung left V20 Gy %, normal < 30%; heart mean dose, constraint < 4 Gy);
Tolerance to Treatment: Observed toxicities with corresponding CTCAE grading and management measures;
Final Treatment Evaluation: Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group (ECOG) performance score; Weight changes; Remaining toxicities;
Future Therapeutic Measures and Follow-up Plans: Anticipated further treatments and follow-up procedures.
